 "long": {
  "title": "I Woke Up in 1828. This Boy Had Never Seen the Sky",
  "description": "Who do you think kept Kaspar Hauser in the dark? Tell me in the comments.\nPrevious true story: https://youtu.be/RU6HcfLCx8w\n\n\"He wrote his own name, and didn't seem to know what it meant.\"\n\nI woke up in Nuremberg on Whit Monday, 26 May 1828, and watched a boy of about 16 stumble into the square with a letter that said: keep him, or hang him. He could say only 'don't know' and 'I want to be a rider like my father'. He said he had spent his life in a dark cell with wooden horses, bread and water, and a keeper he never saw. A hooded attack in 1829, a fatal stabbing in Ansbach in December 1833, a note in mirror writing - and a 2024 DNA study that finally killed the 'stolen prince' theory. Who kept him is still unknown.\n\nSources:\nhttps://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kaspar_Hauser\nhttps://www.britannica.com/biography/Kaspar-hauser\nhttps://www.cell.com/iscience/fulltext/S2589-0042(24)01764-4\nhttps://de.wikisource.org/wiki/ADB:Hauser,_Kaspar\n\n#truestory #kasparhauser #3DAnimation #unsolvedmystery #history",
